' ============================================================
' EPD skeleton (EN 15804+A2)
'
' Work down the file. Every line marked DECIDE needs a decision
' from the practitioner; the comments say what the choice is.
' Run it with:  RUN "my_epd.baslca"
' From Python, Session.run(code, dry_run=True) checks it without
' touching openLCA.
' ============================================================

' DECIDE: which family of names the database uses.
DATABASE FAMILY "ecoinvent"

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' 1. The EPD
' ------------------------------------------------------------
EPD "Product name"
  ' DECIDE: the programme operator. Remove the three lines below to
  ' apply EN 15804+A2 alone. With a programme, its rules are errors.
  PROGRAMME "IES" GPI "5.1.0"
  PCR "Name of the PCR" VERSION "0.0"
  DATABASE "ecoinvent" VERSION "3.11"

  ' DECIDE: the declared unit. FUNCTIONAL UNIT is only for EPD types
  ' with options or cradle to grave.
  DECLARED UNIT 1, kg

  ' The EN 15804+A2 method. The workflow refuses a method with the
  ' wrong number of impact categories.
  METHOD "EN15804+A2 (EF 3.1)"

  ' DECIDE: the folder everything is built in.
  FOLDER "00: Product name EPD"

  ' DECIDE: the modules. A1 to A3, C1 to C4 and D are mandatory.
  ' A4, A5 and B1 to B7 are options.
  MODULES A1, A2, A3, C1, C2, C3, C4, D

  ' DECIDE: does the product contain biogenic carbon? YES or NO.
  ' With YES, give the carbon in the product (and its packaging) per
  ' declared unit, in kg C, or the oven-dry mass of wood. EPD CALCULATE
  ' then checks the carbon balance and refuses a model that does not
  ' close it. A co-product that leaves A1 to A3 with its carbon is
  ' declared with BIOGENIC EXPORT.
  BIOGENIC CARBON NO
  ' BIOGENIC CARBON YES
  ' BIOGENIC CONTENT PRODUCT 0.45 kg C PACKAGING 0 kg C
  ' BIOGENIC CONTENT PRODUCT FROM MASS 0.9 kg DRY
  ' BIOGENIC EXPORT A3 "Sawdust and chips", 0.05 kg C

  ' DECIDE: anything left out of the model is declared here, per
  ' module, as a share of mass or energy.
  ' CUTOFF A3 "Lubricants", 0.2%

  ' Only for a product that meets every condition of the exemption
  ' in EN 15804+A2 clause 5.2: take C1 to C4 and D out of MODULES
  ' and justify it here.
  ' EXEMPT C AND D
  '   INTEGRATED "why the product cannot be separated at end of life"
  '   NOT IDENTIFIABLE "why it is no longer identifiable at end of life"
  '   END OF LIFE SCENARIOS "where the end of life scenarios can be found"
  ' END EXEMPT
END EPD

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' 2. Bridges: one per background dataset, so each choice sits in
'    one place. NEW FROM TEMPLATE "bridges_common" has the patterns.
'    DECIDE: the provider of each (FIND PROCESS gives the UUID).
' ------------------------------------------------------------
' BRIDGE "Raw material", kg
'   PROVIDER "uuid of the background process"
'   DATA SECONDARY SOURCE "Database" PROVIDER "ecoinvent 3.11" YEAR 2024
'   ' DECIDE: how well the dataset stands for what is modelled. The
'   ' levels are Very good, Good, Fair, Poor and Very poor. EPD DATA
'   ' QUALITY needs all three on every dataset that matters.
'   RATING GEOGRAPHY "Good" REASON "why this dataset fits the place"
'   RATING TECHNOLOGY "Good" REASON "why it fits the technology"
'   RATING TIME "Good" REASON "why it fits the period"
' END BRIDGE

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' 3. Modules. Amounts are per declared unit. Inside a module a
'    process is named without its prefix: "Material supply" becomes
'    "A1 | Material supply". Inputs come from bridges or from
'    processes of this EPD.
'    DECIDE for each process: where its data comes from (DATA), and
'    whether the manufacturer controls it (CONTROL). A3 is taken to
'    be under direct control unless a process says CONTROL NONE.
' ------------------------------------------------------------
MODULE A1
  ' MAKE PROCESS "Material supply"
  '   DATA SECONDARY SOURCE "Database" PROVIDER "ecoinvent 3.11" YEAR 2024
  '   OUTPUT MAKE FLOW "Material, supplied", 1, kg, PRODUCT
  '   INPUT USE PROCESS "BRIDGE | Raw material | kg", 1, kg
  ' END PROCESS
  TOTAL "Raw material supply"
END MODULE

MODULE A2
  TOTAL "Transport to the factory"
END MODULE

MODULE A3
  ' MAKE PROCESS "Manufacturing"
  '   DATA PRIMARY SOURCE "Collected" PROVIDER "EPD owner" YEAR 2025
  '   OUTPUT MAKE FLOW "Product, at factory gate", 1, kg, PRODUCT
  '   INPUT USE PROCESS "BRIDGE | Electricity | kWh", 0.5, kWh
  ' END PROCESS
  TOTAL "Manufacturing"
END MODULE

MODULE C1
  TOTAL "Deconstruction"
END MODULE

MODULE C2
  TOTAL "Transport to waste processing"
END MODULE

MODULE C3
  TOTAL "Waste processing"
END MODULE

MODULE C4
  TOTAL "Disposal"
END MODULE

MODULE D
  ' DECIDE: the net flow leaving the product system, and its quality
  ' factor if it is not 100%.
  NET FLOW "Recovered material", 0, kg QUALITY 100%
  TOTAL "Benefits and loads beyond the system boundary"
END MODULE

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' 4. Systems, checks, results. Each step refuses to run until the
'    one before it has passed.
' ------------------------------------------------------------
EPD SYSTEMS
EPD CHECK
EPD CALCULATE

' The register of the datasets the data quality assessment has to
' cover, with the ratings recorded so far. Run it to see what still
' needs a RATING line; add those with EDIT PROCESS and run again.
' EPD DQ SHEET "dq_register.csv"

EPD DATA QUALITY
EPD REPORT "epd_results.csv"

' The assessment table for the accompanying report.
' EPD DQ TABLE "data_quality_assessment.md"

' DECIDE: the parameters to vary together, and by how much.
' EPD SENSITIVITY BY 20% SAVE "sensitivity.csv"
'   GROUP "Electricity" VARY electricity_kwh
'   GROUP "Transport" VARY road_tkm, sea_tkm
' END EPD SENSITIVITY

' The whole model as one file, for the verifier.
' EPD EXPORT MODEL "model.json"

' DECIDE: the EPD document itself, in the programme's sections. Until
' every line below is filled in it is refused; until the statements,
' registration, dates and verification are given it is a draft.
' The statements file is your own copy of the programme's required
' wording (keys: cover, iso14025, operator, ownership, comparability,
' relative, end_of_life, primary_share). HELP EPD DOCUMENT lists it all.
' EPD DOCUMENT "epd.docx"
'   STATEMENTS "ies_statements.txt"
'   OWNER "Company name"
'   OWNER ADDRESS "Street, town, postcode, country"
'   OWNER CONTACT "e-mail"
'   OWNER DESCRIPTION "What the company does"
'   PRODUCT DESCRIPTION "What the product is, its performance and use"
'   PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION "Standard or other identification"
'   MANUFACTURING "The main manufacturing processes"
'   SITE "Town, country"
'   CONTENT "Main material", 1 kg
'   SVHC NONE
'   GEOGRAPHY A1, A2, A3, C1, C2, C3, C4, D "GB"
'   SCENARIO C1, C2, C3, C4, D "The end-of-life scenario"
'   OMITTED A4, A5, B1, B2, B3, B4, B5, B6, B7 "Why they are left out"
' END EPD DOCUMENT

' Once the report is right, EPD SAVE writes the EPD into openLCA as
' well: its own EPD entity with a stored result per module, which can
' be opened, exported and sent on from openLCA.
' EPD SAVE
